    "body": "Hi, I'm coming late… you are mixing await with inline promises, is this on purpose ?\r\n```typescript\r\nasync function sendData(reportData) {\r\n\trecData = [];\r\n\tconst device = await getOpenedDevice();\r\n\tdevice.sendReport(reportId, reportData).then(() => {\r\n\t\tconsole.log('Report Sent')\r\n    });\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI would have written\r\n\r\n```typescript\r\nasync function sendData(reportData) {\r\n\trecData = [];\r\n\tconst device = await getOpenedDevice();\r\n\tawait device.sendReport(reportId, reportData);\r\n        console.log('Report Sent')\r\n}\r\n```\r\nSame for \r\n```typescript\r\ntry {\r\n        const devices = await navigator.hid.requestDevice({\r\n                                    filters: deviceFilters });\r\n        device = devices[0];\r\n        device.open().then(() => {\r\n            device.oninputreport = e => {\r\n                handleInputReport(e);\r\n            }\r\n            //Do something with device here!\r\n        });\r\n```\r\nShould be\r\n\r\n```typescript\r\ntry {\r\n        const devices = await navigator.hid.requestDevice({\r\n                                    filters: deviceFilters });\r\n        device = devices[0];\r\n        await device.open();\r\n        device.oninputreport = e => { handleInputReport(e); }\r\n         //Do something with device here!\r\n...\r\n```\r\n",
